From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Brix Andersen <henrik@brixandersen.dk>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:40:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] usb: device_next: class: gs_usb: send echo frame even on
 failed CAN TX

Send a host echo frame even on a failed CAN TX in order to free the URB
used in the Linux kernel gs_usb driver.

Going forward, a new echo frame flag needs to be introduced for indicating
dropped CAN frames successfully delivered via USB but dropped by the CAN
controller/firmware.

Signed-off-by: Henrik Brix Andersen <henrik@brixandersen.dk>
(cherry picked from commit 9cb0d9020b131e04ac916ae8f71c7dd0f85f79d2)
---
 subsys/usb/device_next/class/gs_usb.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/subsys/usb/device_next/class/gs_usb.c b/subsys/usb/device_next/class/gs_usb.c
index 5145ac0..9ffa07c 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/device_next/class/gs_usb.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/device_next/class/gs_usb.c
@@ -1168,10 +1168,8 @@ static void gs_usb_can_tx_callback(const struct device *can_dev, int error, void
 	uint8_t *tail;
 
 	if (error != 0) {
-		/* There is no way to report a dropped frame to the host driver */
+		/* There is currently no way to report a dropped frame to the host driver */
 		LOG_ERR("failed to send CAN frame (err %d)", error);
-		net_buf_unref(buf);
-		return;
 	}
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_USBD_GS_USB_TIMESTAMP
